From ecb73710bf2bc66ca1fc81c1f8495088c9b7b3e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:22:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] fix(app): read a 3+2 plane and a cross drill through
 every table pose

The post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the move with the
rotary words. On a machine whose table tilts the work, the X/Y traverse
of a 3+2 plane or a cross drill runs at the pose the previous program
left. The posed law of #3084 now reads those kinds too (posed_kind),
and reads the fixed machine table when only the work tilts.

The first_traverse_table test of a trunnion now expects the verdict of
the block on its sphere (decision 3100).

Fixes #3100

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
